<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Judicate of Arborea</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 CE – 1420 CE (approx.) · capital Oristano</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Longest-lived of Sardinia's four judicates, centred on Oristano, whose Eleanor of Arborea issued the Carta de Logu law code in Sardinian.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Arborea emerged in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-oristano">Gulf of Oristano</a>, as one of the four judicates that replaced Byzantine rule in the 10th and 11th centuries. Its capital moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharros">Tharros</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oristano">Oristano</a> around 1070.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Arborea was a kingdom in all but name, ruled by judges with a council of notables. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisone-ii-of-arborea">Barisone II</a> was crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in 1164. In the 14th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-iv-of-arborea">Mariano IV</a> fought the Aragonese conquest, and his daughter Eleanor issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu">Carta de Logu</a> in 1392, a law code in Sardinian that remained in force across the island until 1827. Its economy rested on grain, herding and salt.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Arborea's army was defeated by the Aragonese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sanluri">Sanluri</a> in 1409. In 1420 William III of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viscounty-of-narbonne">Narbonne</a>, the last claimant, sold his remaining rights to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a> for 100,000 gold florins, and Arborea became the Marquisate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oristano">Oristano</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/judicate-of-arborea.jpg" alt="Judicate of Arborea" width="320" height="201"><figcaption>Image: Fabiocarboni; derivative work by The White Lion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Giudicato_of_Arborea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 CE – 1420 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Oristano</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Barisone II, Mariano IV, Eleanor of Arborea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sardinian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Giudicato di Arborea, Kingdom of Arborea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1210&amp;focus=judicate-of-arborea" aria-label="Judicate of Arborea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4892 750 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Judicate of Arborea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5212 1006L5226 1028M5212 1006L5206 976"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5226 1028h0M5206 976h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5212 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5212 1006h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Oristano. <a href="/atlas?year=1210&amp;focus=judicate-of-arborea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

